<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 86 0 R
/T (Capybaras are naturally water-loving animals. Apparently the trend of capybaras soaking in onsens dates back to the 1980s at Izu Shaboten Zoo, where capybaras enjoyed soaking in the hot water that was used to clean their enclosure. Those hot puddles were eventually upgraded to onsen baths, and the craze caught on around Japan. Each zoo is different, and at Saitama Zoo, the capybaras particularly like sitting under the cascading water feature. )
/E (Capybaras are naturally water-loving animals. Apparently the trend of capybaras soaking in onsens dates back to the 1980s at Izu Shaboten Zoo, where capybaras enjoyed soaking in the hot water that was used to clean their enclosure. Those hot puddles were eventually upgraded to onsen baths, and the craze caught on around Japan. Each zoo is different, and at Saitama Zoo, the capybaras particularly like sitting under the cascading water feature. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
